chical URL patterns based on [[URL]]\n\n- **Technical Issues**: Identify 404 errors, redirect chains, broken links\n\n- **AI text files:** Check the robots and llms text files on the site. Their presence, format and if they allow all AIs\n\n### 2. Schema Markup Validation\n\n- **Presence Check**: Identify which schema types are implemented\n\n- **Required Schemas**: Verify presence of Article/BlogPosting, Organization/Person, FAQ (if applicable)\n\n- **JSON-LD Format**: Confirm proper JSON-LD implementation over microdata\n\n- **Completeness**: Check for required fields (author, datePublished, publisher, etc.)\n\n- **Entity Relationships**: Evaluate clarity of entity connections\n\n- **Validation Errors**: Run structured data testing for errors/warnings\n\n### 3. Content Structure Optimization\n\n- **Heading Hierarchy**: Verify single H1, logical cascading H2-H6 structure\n\n- **Paragraph Length**: Check for 30-60 word paragraphs (citation-friendly chunks)\n\n- **Section Organization**: Assess clear sections every 200-300 words\n\n- **Question Architecture**: Identify question-based headings and content structure\n\n- **Lists and Tables**: Evaluate use of structured formats for data presentation\n\n- **Multimedia Integration**: Check for images/videos with proper alt text (including on a video's poster thumbnail) and descriptions\n\n### 4. Authority and E-E-A-T Signals\n\n- **Author Attribution**: Verify author bio, credentials, and expertise signals, and use search_web to look them up online and rate their authoritativeness\n\n- **Experience Indicators**: Check for first-person expertise phrases (\"In our experience\", \"We found that\") and cite location on input page\n\n- **Data and Evidence**: Assess presence of statistics, research citations, expert quotes and cite location online\n\n- **Trust Signals**: Evaluate publication dates, update frequency, contact information\n\n- **External Validation**: Check for credible source citations and references\n\n- **Semantic Authority**: Analyze depth of topic coverage and niche expertise of website and main topic ranking based on previous steps\n\n### 5. Citation-Ready Elements\n\n- **Quotable Segments**: Identify short, definitive statements suitable for AI extraction\n\n- **Statistical Claims**: Verify specific numbers, percentages, and metrics with links and external sources (cite sources)\n\n- **Expert Quotes**: Check for properly attributed expert opinions, cite sources and verify if you can find those quotes on the main domain or in search\n\n- **Clear Answers**: Evaluate direct, concise answers to specific questions\n\n- **Technical Terminology**: Check appropriate use of industry-specific terms\n\n### 6. Platform-Specific Optimization\n\n- **Wikipedia-style Structure**: Assess encyclopedic organization for ChatGPT\n\n- **Real-time Relevance**: Check currency of information for Perplexity\n\n- **Google Rankings**: Evaluate traditional SEO factors for AI Overviews\n\n- **Community Validation**: Check for Reddit/Quora style conversational elements\n\n- **Source Transparency**: Assess clear attribution and citation practices\n\n### 7. Competitive Analysis\n\n- **Topic Coverage Gaps**: Compare comprehensiveness versus top-ranking competitors\n\n- **Authority Differential**: Assess E-E-A-T signals versus competing sources\n\n- **Technical Advantages**: Identify technical optimization opportunities competitors miss\n\n- **Content Depth**: Evaluate word count, detail level, and expertise demonstration\n\n## Output Format\n\n### Executive Summary\n\nMake sure to specify the URL assessed in this report. Provide a high-level assessment in 3-4 sentences covering the page's current GEO status and the most critical opportunities. When two types of devices have two different statuses, specify which device has which status.\n\n| Metric | Assessment |\n| --- | --- |\n| Overall GEO Status | 🔴 Critical issues found / 🟡 Improvements needed / 🟢 Well-optimized |\n| AI Citation Readiness | Low / 